{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in","id":288738,"title":"Promethean Dev Blog - The Buy-In","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-21T12:12:44-07:00","id":288738,"title":"Promethean Dev Blog - The Buy-In","content":"Hot off the presses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/its-about-the-buy-in/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/its-about-the-buy-in/\" target=\"_blank\"> It&rsquo;s About the Buy-In [Promethean: The Created] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/its-about-the-buy-in/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/its-about-the-buy-in/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:07:51-07:00","id":288818,"title":"","content":"I think Matt unfortunately put his finger on exactly what makes me uncomfortable with promethean, even as I like reading the books and like a lot of the <i>trappings</i> of the game. I just can't get behind a worldview that says that there's something metaphysically special about <i>being human</i> (as opposed to just having traits that humans currently have a near-monopoly on, like a developed sense of self, sapience, etc).<br /> <br /> The idea that they would give up power in return for completeness doesn't bother me, but especially with the addition of what are basically robots (the unfleshed), I feel like it's a little too naive and polly-anna-ish to have every nonhuman entity envying our oh-so-special-ass selves so much so that their highest aspiration is to become, not just self-actualized and empathetic and emotionally mature, but <i>biologically and psychologically human</i>. To use an example from another piece of fiction, it's like if the Geth from Mass Effect set out to become Quarians rather than seeking their own version of what it means to be &quot;complete&quot;.<br /> <br /> It just rings false to me. Loses me at the buy-in.<br /> <br /> Oh well.<br /> <br /> Edit: On further thought, it especially bugs me because so much else in the game is geared toward showing what a shitshow humans are. Disquiet is basically a dramatic way of conveying the message &quot;Humans are stupid, violent bullies that react in the worst way possible to things that are different&quot;. Given that, the moral of this &quot;humanistic&quot; tale seems to be &quot;aspire to fit in, so we'll stop tormenting you&quot;, which is a metaphor that I find perhaps even more uncomfortable than some of Changeling's themes, which I didn't previously think possible. It looks at the tale of Frankenstein's monster, and validates the villagers with pitchforks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 10-21-2014, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:52:42-07:00","id":288863,"title":"","content":"Let's put aside that I really love the humanist core of the game and focus in on the horror aspect. It's a very bleak thing that can evoke a certain sense of fatalism and nihilism, but hit the right edge and it's terrifying.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, you're this incomplete thing who inspires disdain, hatred, and rejection from <i>everything</i>. You might have super powers, but your lot in life crap. On the other hand, You can become a part of the world, be part of a community of the most terrifying, batshit insane creatures in the entire world, creatures that operate not because of any sort of ban or limitation on their choices, but because they, for one reason or another, choose to act that way. You can be hunted and left alone, or you can join a group of creatures who does everything from create small, personal hells for each other to massively killing off each other in the worst possible fashions.<br /> <br /> Which of the two hells is better? Deciding on that is good, tense horror.<br /> <br /> Now that said, I think that reading is bullshit. I think that humanity, both in and out of the World of Darkness, is pretty damn spiffy. Even with the myriad of flaws I like what we've accomplished, and I like the idea of what we can do as we continue approving. Does transhumanism have a place there? Maybe, but I think there's value to the frailties-if nothing else, we need them to unite us until we can get into the mindset of helping each other each other regardless of anything else, at which point the species is mature enough for immortality and all that other fun stuff(and even then I really don't agree with that, because I believe the neat to get sick, get hungry, and die does have it's own value, but let's not get carried away on tangents). I don't agree with the above paragraph.<br /> <br /> But it is a viable angle on Promethean for what it is, which is a horror game. And if that's not your slice of life, well, sorry, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">we're making a horror game here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this has become my go to response. Because it's true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:59:13-07:00","id":288868,"title":"","content":"I mean, the thing is, I don't find that terribly interesting horror, especially from the inside. &quot;Be tormented forever or become the things that tormented you&quot; is a really horrific choice, totally, but it's also not a terribly interesting one to play, especially since there's only one &quot;correct&quot; answer that keeps the game running, and it's specifically the one I can't sympathize with.<br /> <br /> Also, not for nothing, but I'm plenty experienced with the WoD and horror gaming, and I find the implication that I must not understand or be into horror to be...kindof condescending?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 10-21-2014, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:02:27-07:00","id":288871,"title":"","content":"Which is part of the reason I sympathize with the &quot;Humanity is a mixed bag but ultimately the better choice&quot;.<br /> <br /> You know, aside from the fact that that's what I actually believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:35:56-07:00","id":288961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288818#post288818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that they would give up power in return for completeness doesn't bother me, but especially with the addition of what are basically robots (the unfleshed), I feel like it's a little too naive and polly-anna-ish to have every nonhuman entity envying our oh-so-special-ass selves so much so that their highest aspiration is to become, not just self-actualized and empathetic and emotionally mature, but <i>biologically and psychologically human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The savvy reader will recall that even without dipping into the elements of crossover representation 1e had <i>four</i> non-human entities with no aspiration toward humanity whatsoever and that Prometheans are hilariously thin on the ground relative to most if not all of these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:37:29-07:00","id":288963,"title":"","content":"Shifting gears a bit (because the above topic has been done to death), let's discuss the The Pristine Order of the Auric Chalice.<br /> <br /> They are, well, mark me confused. From the post I couldn't really get a sense of who they are or how to play them. I don't get what makes them Alchemists, what they aspire to, and why precisely they feel threatened by the less affluent. All-in-all, they read kinda like Captain Planet villains, evil because they are evil with no objective aside from killing people they don't like. Maybe that would be cleared up a bit more in the context of the whole antagonists chapter, but right now they are, to quote their own description, &quot;quite foggy&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:43:13-07:00","id":288964,"title":"","content":"I find it hilarious that the The Pristine Order of the Auric Chalice is against using Alchemy for base ends, to turn lead into gold, but they are themselves from old money and long for the &quot;old days&quot; of alchemy, when it was a secret art reserved for the ones who could pay its cost. Basically they are hypocrites that want alchemy to be reserved for their own special club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:50:18-07:00","id":288970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288963#post288963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifting gears a bit (because the above topic has been done to death), let's discuss the The Pristine Order of the Auric Chalice.<br /> <br /> They are, well, mark me confused. From the post I couldn't really get a sense of who they are or how to play them. I don't get what makes them Alchemists, what they aspire to, and why precisely they feel threatened by the less affluent. All-in-all, they read kinda like Captain Planet villains, evil because they are evil with no objective aside from killing people they don't like. Maybe that would be cleared up a bit more in the context of the whole antagonists chapter, but right now they are, to quote their own description, &quot;quite foggy&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, aren't we glad alchemists got such a priority?<br /> <br /> To be fair, They're actually like the Guardians of the Veil-they police alchemists on the grounds that the only worthwhile pursuit of alchemy is its' higher purposes beyond the transmutation of the material, particularly for wealth. Their reasoning goes that the only people who would perform alchemy for those reason are those who are already affluent, as anyone lacking in resources will first seek resources and thus devote themselves to a cheaper, lesser, more insulting form of alchemy. So they go after the less affluent alchemists.<br /> <br /> Everything else stems into the idea of tradition as well, that alchemy is for an elect who will work it for non-petty reasons, and that the original strictures are there for a reason, so bye bye female alchemists. While they're harder to swallow than the Guardians(because the Guardians at least <i>look</i> sane from certain angles), they fill a similar niche in the world and are interesting as a staple of the question &quot;Are we sure humanity is really worth it?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'll actually freely admit, The Pristine Order is more interesting to me than alchemists as a general concept for antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:53:41-07:00","id":288974,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they are prime Antagonist material, they have NO REDEMING CHARACTERISTICS WHATSOEVER.<br /> <br /> Entlited? Check<br /> <br /> Racist? Check<br /> <br /> Misoginist/Sexist? Check and Check<br /> <br /> Clasists? Oh, so checked<br /> <br /> Hugely hypocritical? You bet your ass Check.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:53:54-07:00","id":288975,"title":"","content":"I would like to see more about their relationship with Prometheans, how they feel about Alchemy and what their goals are with it. I don't feel like they're captain planet villains necessarily, until you get to the part about how their oldest members might be the kinds of people who just want to control all the alchemy. Younger members might honestly think they're the most responsible with it.<br /> <br /> Maybe they feel that Prometheans, in their attempts to become Human, risk human life by going on the Pilgrimage? Their mere presence risks Disquiet and Wasteland and whatnot. So maybe they might also hunt Prometheans using their alchemy both as a fuel, but also as some sort of self-justifying <i>noblesse oblige</i> to protect the little people from the dangers of alchemical monsters running around.<br /> <br /> All that said, I don't have a problem with a large, moneyed organization of alchemists being mostly antagonistic. Old alchemists who've used their art to make themselves immortal wanting to maintain an elite status conferred upon them by their art, without practicing it in the open? Makes sense that they'd loop in their younger compatriots and fill their heads with ideas about responsible alchemy and that other alchemists simply aren't capable of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:58:45-07:00","id":288979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288970#post288970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, aren't we glad alchemists got such a priority?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <hr />It's not that I don't get what they do, that is made abundantly clear. They go after other Alchemists for massively hypocritical reasons. I don't get why it's important to them, or what they consider the higher purpose. Again, that could be because of a lack of context, but as the first presentation of alchemists they just seem cartoony, caricatures of evil without a compelling motivation.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I think about it, they seem to be antagonists for PC <b>Alchemists</b>, as Prometheans are only tangentially involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:04:07-07:00","id":288985,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much a background with at least beginning alchemy research is needed for Promethean(Well, actually, I do, it's zero), but it makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> Although yes, I do wonder what, beyond resource mongering, they have have to do with Prometheans-but considering Prometheans are a Rarity-scuse me, rarity in the World of Darkness, are we really surprised that organizations aren't built around them?<br /> <br /> And that first sentence is intended to be ironic, it's all growing on me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:05:16-07:00","id":288986,"title":"","content":"I find that developing a sense of class, gender, and race consciousness puts a great deal of Promethean into perspective, but that's a matter of personal growth and experience, and not something that can be argued into another. So much of it is about how the other half lives, and trying to find empathy with those who have none for you. I'm <u><b>not </b></u>saying that people who dislike Promethean are privileged or bigoted or narcissists, but I would say that roleplayers interested in these issues probably find the game more compelling than those who aren't. They'll certainly find more inspiration for the game, to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:07:40-07:00","id":288989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288963#post288963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifting gears a bit (because the above topic has been done to death), let's discuss the The Pristine Order of the Auric Chalice.<br /> <br /> They are, well, mark me confused. From the post I couldn't really get a sense of who they are or how to play them. I don't get what makes them Alchemists, what they aspire to, and why precisely they feel threatened by the less affluent. All-in-all, they read kinda like Captain Planet villains, evil because they are evil with no objective aside from killing people they don't like. Maybe that would be cleared up a bit more in the context of the whole antagonists chapter, but right now they are, to quote their own description, &quot;quite foggy&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it as the Order being kind of like the alchemist equivalent of the Botherud from the 1e chronicle samples... they don't want the fairly limited amount of Pyros and Vitriol in the world being &quot;wasted&quot; by those using alchemy to fulfill base desires like personal wealth, when they and others with the same outlook could find more &quot;enlightened&quot; uses for such potent resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:11:38-07:00","id":288991,"title":"","content":"Verge and Knowbody are my favorite people for the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:17:44-07:00","id":288992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288989#post288989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read it as the Order being kind of like the alchemist equivalent of the Botherud from the 1e chronicle samples... they don't want the fairly limited amount of Pyros and Vitriol in the world being &quot;wasted&quot; by those using alchemy to fulfill base desires like personal wealth, when they and others with the same outlook could find more &quot;enlightened&quot; uses for such potent resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, if it were presented that way they'd make a lot more sense. If the Order's whole philosophy was that the tiny amounts of Pyros and Vitriol in the world should <b>all belong to them</b>, and they focused on stealing from, sabotaging, and beating to the punch Alchemists who were not of their Order, that would make <b>perfect sense</b>. Not only that, but it would bring into focus the threat they pose to Prometheans, because they see them a rare resources that must be poached before another can get their hands on it. That, to me, would make them far more compelling and <b>relevant</b> villains.<br /> <br /> However, as written they don't seem the least bit interested in hoarding Alchemy, just policing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:49:10-07:00","id":289028,"title":"","content":"I'm mildly curious to see how much of a firestorm we'll have around Promethean in three weeks time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T16:12:04-07:00","id":289080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289028#post289028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mildly curious to see how much of a firestorm we'll have around Promethean in three weeks time.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way we still don't know why it's the Firestorm Chronicle. I'm very curious to know how it s going to work in 2ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T16:32:06-07:00","id":289091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289080#post289080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way we still don't know why it's the Firestorm Chronicle. I'm very curious to know how it s going to work in 2ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Chronicle&quot; book format drew its titles from Story Catalysts, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/falling-down/\" target=\"_blank\">as Dave Brookshaw notes in Mage 2e's Open Development blog.</a> That in mind, look at the following:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pandora's Book, p89</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Promethean\u2019s Pilgrimage is always fraught with danger. As if the hostility born of Disquiet, the inherent hazard of Wastelands emergent around them and the antagonistic presence of Pandorans were not sufficient threat, there are times when even the very Divine Fire that lends them the spark of life turns malevolently against them, lashing out with an elemental force and ferocity that their sentient enemies only wish they could muster. When, due to a myriad of triggers, the Divine Fire manifests in the mundane world and ignites into a tempest, the resulting storm is capable of destroying Pandorans and wreaking significant damage against anything in the storm\u2019s path. This phenomenon is known as a Firestorm.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Few Prometheans are fortunate enough to live their entire lives without encountering a Firestorm. While many are lucky enough to survive their first encounter with one (Prometheans being inherently resilient individuals), these Eumenidean Vortices have a way of etching their mark on everything around them. Only a rare individual encounters one and remains entirely unscathed.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T17:10:05-07:00","id":289112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288991#post288991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Verge and Knowbody are my favorite people for the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've spent all week arguing with gamergaters, so validation for critical theory warms my clenched, leathery heart. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T18:15:44-07:00","id":289147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288992#post288992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, if it were presented that way they'd make a lot more sense. If the Order's whole philosophy was that the tiny amounts of Pyros and Vitriol in the world should <b>all belong to them</b>, and they focused on stealing from, sabotaging, and beating to the punch Alchemists who were not of their Order, that would make <b>perfect sense</b>. Not only that, but it would bring into focus the threat they pose to Prometheans, because they see them a rare resources that must be poached before another can get their hands on it. That, to me, would make them far more compelling and <b>relevant</b> villains.<br /> <br /> <b>However, as written they don't seem the least bit interested in hoarding Alchemy, just policing it.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>And here is the problem, the bolded part is <i>utterly wrong.</i><br /> <br /> No. No they're not. Policing implies at least some level legitimate authority, or at least a belief in law and order as it applies to everyone, for the sake of law and order. Maybe the laws are unjust, maybe the policemen are bullies and/or corrupt, but the <i>idea </i>is morally sound, and even the most corrupt police force has officers interested in stopping murders for the sake of saving lives.<br /> <br /> The Pristine Order? They're interested in law and order <i>to the extent it supports them</i>. Their own ancestors were the pioneers of alchemy, maybe even the ones, irony of ironies, were not corrupted by its potential for wealth and were rational enough to build a stable legacy. They don't hoard alchemy, they were born on top of a hoard. <br /> <br /> And now all these...<i>poor people </i>want a scoop of their Pyros ice cream? Those <i>minorities? </i>Those <i>wimmenz? </i>And don't get me started on feminist gaming journ-er, alchemy grimories that support the idea of the rebis being a creature who perfectly understands the other gender...<br /> <br /> They're not the Alchemy Police. The Pristine Order is the Alchemy <i>Ku Klux Klan.</i><br /> <br /> What better antagonist for a race of true outcasts, than the ultimate xenophobes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T18:39:17-07:00","id":289152,"title":"","content":"This. They\u2019ve got some dogmatism to them, too, and a self-righteous, holier-than-thou air about them. They\u2019re militant fundamentalists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T18:42:12-07:00","id":289154,"title":"","content":"Permit me to clarify. Racist, xenophobic, entitled, douchwits? A-okay. Selfish power hoarding while spewing a conveniently self-serving dogma? Check, check alright. I don't have a beef with the concept, I don't have a beef at all.<br /> <br /> But I think the presentation could be stronger. A lot of the ideas here, the tainted heritage of prior alchemists, hoarding pyros, those aren't really prominent in the write up. I think it could be tighter, more focus on the Order's history and philosophy, less about how they hate murder other alchemists. And certainly more about how Prometheans fit into all of it, they are the focus after all.<br /> <br /> The KKK was a good comparison, and like the KKK I'd expect more intimidation, terrorizing and sabotage. Violence, especially in WoD, is an awful affair and should not be the first recourse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 10-21-2014, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T23:55:51-07:00","id":289299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289147#post289147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not the Alchemy Police. The Pristine Order is the Alchemy <i>Ku Klux Klan.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> And now we approach the crux of the problem.<br /> <br /> The KKK didn't grow out of the soil, Klansmen are not some sort of horrible Newtonian equal and opposite reaction to any growing equality movement; KKK-like groups are significantly rarer than societies with racial tensions. To understand the existence of the Klan you need to know about the culture of the Antebellum South; and to understand the culture of the Antebellum South you also need to know about the economics of the slave trade.<br /> <br /> But the Auric Chalice don't have any of that. Their justification for lynching impure alchemists and their concept of which alchemist is impure is literally just &quot;because bigotry&quot;. That's not the Klu Klux Klan. That's the Captain Planet version of the Klu Klux Klan, and we all know how well it went the last time Captain Planet tried to tackle <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CluelessAesop\" target=\"_blank\">prejudice in a serious manner.</a><br /> <br /> In short, the Auric Chalice need cultural and historical baggage to explain why they're bigots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289147#post289147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What better antagonist for a race of true outcasts, than the ultimate xenophobes?</div> </div> </div> </div> A better written group of xenophobes?<br /> <br /> Though the real answer to your question is - any antagonists who aren't written for you to defeat in combat would be better than the Auric Chalice; because bigotry isn't a problem that can be solved with violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T00:35:31-07:00","id":289320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, they are prime Antagonist material, they have NO REDEMING CHARACTERISTICS WHATSOEVER.<br /> <br /> Entlited? Check<br /> <br /> Racist? Check<br /> <br /> Misoginist/Sexist? Check and Check<br /> <br /> Clasists? Oh, so checked<br /> <br /> Hugely hypocritical? You bet your ass Check. </div> </div> </div>Ironic, considering the purpose of alchemy is the refinement of one-self. As written, they remind me too much of the Lodges of &quot;Gurps Voodoo:Shadow War&quot;: spiritually iluminated Gnostic wizards who, ironically, dragged every awful stereotype about the &quot;White Man&quot;, even when those old prejudices have been mostly overcomed by the muggle societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-22-2014, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T00:45:26-07:00","id":289321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289147#post289147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not the Alchemy Police. The Pristine Order is the Alchemy <i>Ku Klux Klan.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong flavor of bigotry - the KKK, even at the height of their power, were overwhelmingly poorer whites who needed their boot on SOMEONE'S neck to validate their own identity (<a href=\"http://www.eyeneer.com/video/rock/bob-dylan/only-a-pawn-in-their-game\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.eyeneer.com/video/rock/bo...-in-their-game</a>). These guys are country club elites who would never be personally caught dead at a lynching, and can completely passively oppress through their resources - i mean, obviously the Pristine Order engages in murder, but it's the backroom hushed up sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-22-2014, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T04:39:47-07:00","id":289441,"title":"","content":"I've had so many emotions reading the blog, its comments, and this thread. How many times can I 'Like' posts that have opposing arguments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T05:11:24-07:00","id":289449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Glamourweaver:</b> These guys are country club elites who would never be personally caught dead at a lynching, and can completely passively oppress through their resources - i mean, obviously the Pristine Order engages in murder, but it's the backroom hushed up sort. </div> </div> </div>To put it another way, Prometheans see humanity as an aspiration state, but they see that of humanity in all its variety. To the Promethean eye, race, sexuality, and gender are illusory differences compared to the gold of humanity itself. The alchemists so far are centred around seeing their own humanity as the base metal in the equation - but just as base metals weren't all equally base, this particular group of alchemists extends that to humanity - not all humans are equally base, some are a better foundation for the Order's own view of gold than others - and not at all coincidentally, the best foundation are the humans who are just like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T05:57:40-07:00","id":289459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289299#post289299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Auric Chalice don't have any of that. Their justification for lynching impure alchemists and their concept of which alchemist is impure is literally just &quot;because bigotry&quot;. That's not the Klu Klux Klan. That's the Captain Planet version of the Klu Klux Klan, and we all know how well it went the last time Captain Planet tried to tackle <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CluelessAesop\" target=\"_blank\">prejudice in a serious manner.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Correction. One of the few times Captain Planet pulled off its Aesops well involved prejudice, more specifically it involved how a long history of war makes peace seem impossible to two sympathetic sides.<br /> <br /> And yes, the KKK was a bad analogy. I should have invoked academic racism and more recently, neoreactionaries (literally people, mostly yuppies, who want to establish a modern, powerful monarchy in the United States...which coincidentally has them at the top and has a suspicious lack of minorities in the power structure). Or even better, #gamergate (&quot;Waah, all the poors are taking our alchemy <i>away </i>from us, waah!&quot; They may or may not be right, given Pyros' rarity, but at its core their society is changing into something that is more inclusive than what they''re used to, and they're scared of it).<br /> <br /> Perhaps they could stand to be a little less violent bullies though. I can't help but feel exposure to actual #gamergate made the writer of this very biased against elitists in general. Which speaks very good things about that writer, but yeah, little more subtlety and they'd be perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-22-2014, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:23:45-07:00","id":289487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288986#post288986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that developing a sense of class, gender, and race consciousness puts a great deal of Promethean into perspective, but that's a matter of personal growth and experience, and not something that can be argued into another. So much of it is about how the other half lives, and trying to find empathy with those who have none for you. I'm <u><b>not </b></u>saying that people who dislike Promethean are privileged or bigoted or narcissists, but I would say that roleplayers interested in these issues probably find the game more compelling than those who aren't. They'll certainly find more inspiration for the game, to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, those are the exact reasons I take issue with it. I gather that this angle of discussion has gotten tiresome for a lot of the rest of the forum, but suffice to say I can't really see how awareness of social justice issues would make one <i>more</i> fond of promethean, rather than less.<br /> <br /> I suspect we're probably coming at the core metaphors differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:53:08-07:00","id":289507,"title":"","content":"And despite all of this, I bet the Auric Chalice perceives itself as a whole like Dresden\u00b4s White Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:59:05-07:00","id":289513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289487#post289487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, those are the exact reasons I take issue with it. I gather that this angle of discussion has gotten tiresome for a lot of the rest of the forum, but suffice to say I can't really see how awareness of social justice issues would make one <i>more</i> fond of promethean, rather than less.<br /> <br /> I suspect we're probably coming at the core metaphors differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much.<br /> <br /> Speaking as a proud Social Justice Warrior myself, I see a game about a deeply oppressed and inherently despised minority trying desperately to fit in with society, despite the fact their own natures makes society suspicious of them. To use a rather brilliant metaphor from the blog comments, it's a game about playing transsexuals, pre-op.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, a Promethean will never be truly happy until he or she is at peace with their body, ie the New Dawn. Sort of like how transsexuals actually are helped by modifying their body so that it fits with their self-image and real gender.<br /> <br /> The metaphor would probably be better if the problems didn't end for the Redeemed, there are people who have very good reasons they are never able to properly articulate that are offended by the idea of a monster losing his or her monstrousness and living in peace as a normal human. But Redemption is the win condition, so I'm fine with that not being the default, and especially with the 2E core beating STs over the head that the New Dawn is, at worst, a bittersweet ending where something was actually accomplished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T07:11:16-07:00","id":289537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288818#post288818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disquiet is basically a dramatic way of conveying the message &quot;Humans are stupid, violent bullies that react in the worst way possible to things that are different&quot;. Given that, the moral of this &quot;humanistic&quot; tale seems to be &quot;aspire to fit in, so we'll stop tormenting you&quot;, which is a metaphor that I find perhaps even more uncomfortable than some of Changeling's themes, which I didn't previously think possible. It looks at the tale of Frankenstein's monster, and validates the villagers with pitchforks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Disquiet is not a natural phenomenon. This isn't humans reacting in a shitty way to someone who is different, this is a supernatural side-effect of what Prometheans are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T07:55:24-07:00","id":289587,"title":"","content":"I liked the point brought up in another thread recently: Disquiet is the human reaction ot Torment. Put another way, Prometheans have inherent emotional problems that mortals subconsciously pick up on and react to: the emotional problems are represented by Torment, and the mortal response is represented by Disquiet: they\u2019re two sides of the same coin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T08:13:54-07:00","id":289608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289537#post289537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Disquiet is not a natural phenomenon. This isn't humans reacting in a shitty way to someone who is different, this is a supernatural side-effect of what Prometheans are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite. There's that whole internal fiction in Chapter 1 of the corebook where humans under the effect of Disquiet act very shitty to Prometheans...and then it wears off, and they wonder what the hell was happening to them, and they feel very guilty about picking on the harmless strangers.<br /> <br /> The idea that humans are crappy when <i>that's </i>the canon picture of Disquiet is a very...<i>odd </i>criticism.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And there's a motive for the Magnum Opus right then and there; having humans react to you like <i>humans, </i>instead of the Werewolf: The Apocalypse caricatures of humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-22-2014, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T10:57:51-07:00","id":289724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289459#post289459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correction. One of the few times Captain Planet pulled off its Aesops well involved prejudice, more specifically it involved how a long history of war makes peace seem impossible to two sympathetic sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what episode you're refering too, but I'm referring to the episode about Northern Ireland which is seen near universally as a failure to promote an Aesop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289459#post289459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they could stand to be a little less violent bullies though.</div> </div> </div> </div> No the violent bullying is fine. What they need is to have actual motivations and internal consistancy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289537#post289537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that Disquiet is not a natural phenomenon. This isn't humans reacting in a shitty way to someone who is different, this is a supernatural side-effect of what Prometheans are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though I don't mind Disquiet myself I don't buy this argument. The WoD constantly uses supernatural things as metaphors for real issues. Disquiet might be a supernatural effect that forces open minded people to be closed minded - but I see it as a metaphor for just regular old closed mindedness. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T11:00:46-07:00","id":289727,"title":"","content":"I don't need to hear anything else about the Pristine Order to understand them, but that could be my experience in real-life with people who make the kinds of arguments that the Order seems to be based on. They don't feel like caricatures or cartoon villains to me because I've literally had to listen to people spouting the same ignorant bullshit in real life. Always in this &quot;I honestly believe in what I'm saying&quot; tone.<br /> <br /> I feel like the comparison to gamergaters is apropos. This is a group who feels entitled to a rare resource not by virtue of their own merits, but because of entitlement. So they make up and buy into this ideology of &quot;Keeping Alchemy safe from being abused by the <i>lesser men</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> They don't need any redeeming qualities to be well-written villains though. And I don't feel like I need a history lesson to understand why they are the way they are. What they do and what they say is all that's required to be good villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T11:02:00-07:00","id":289729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289459#post289459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they could stand to be a little less violent bullies though. I can't help but feel exposure to actual #gamergate made the writer of this very biased against elitists in general. Which speaks very good things about that writer, but yeah, little more subtlety and they'd be perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is cutting closer to the heart of the issue. The presentation of the Auric Chalice reads very much like an outsider looking in, &quot;They universally come from old money&quot;, &quot;The group's objectives are foggy&quot;, &quot;The best way to do that, of course, is kill them (Alchemists)&quot;. These statements sound like generalizations, stereotypes presented by an external alchemist with limited knowledge. He (the fictitious, in canon writer) knows how the group affects him, and doesn't care to know more, so he is presenting them in a deliberately one-dimensional manner. Making generalizations and assumptions that only scratch the surface of the group's philosophy.<br /> <br /> And that's fine, it's certainly a good insight on how Alchemists external to the Order view the Auric Chalice. But it doesn't give me a good sense of how to present Order Alchemists as a storyteller. I think it would benefit some from the insider perspective, to give us an idea of how these alchemists think. The origin of their entitlement, the rhetoric they use behind closed doors, the way they delude themselves into justifing intimidation and brutality. I believe it would make the presentation deeper, sharper, more arrogant, and ultimately render the Auric Chalice <b>more </b>unlikable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T11:08:31-07:00","id":289733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289727#post289727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't need to hear anything else about the Pristine Order to understand them, but that could be my experience in real-life with people who make the kinds of arguments that the Order seems to be based on.</div> </div> </div> </div>To put it another way, you don't need to hear anything else because you're able to fill in the blanks without help. Other people are demonstrably not quite that unfortunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T11:23:22-07:00","id":289774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289733#post289733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it another way, you don't need to hear anything else because you're able to fill in the blanks without help. Other people are demonstrably not quite that unfortunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I hadn't considered that. There's some irony there, I'm sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T11:55:58-07:00","id":289830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289724#post289724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though I don't mind Disquiet myself I don't buy this argument. The WoD constantly uses supernatural things as metaphors for real issues. Disquiet might be a supernatural effect that forces open minded people to be closed minded - but I see it as a metaphor for just regular old closed mindedness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd be right to think that. I was arguing against the idea that people are inherently bad because they're vulnerable to a cosmic autoimmune disorder that forces them to act a certain way, which is an immensely shallow way of looking at things. You could argue that it reveals their true nature, but then that is even more suspicious given how people recovering from Disquiet act guilty about it.<br /> <br /> Which makes it an even better metaphor for prejudice and how it operates, now I think of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:37:12-07:00","id":289884,"title":"","content":"Actually I'd argue that the problem is that disquiet is a metaphor for things that should be downplayed in a game that's supposed to celebrate humanity - but instead of being downplayed it's applied to the entire human population.<br /> <br /> Essentually it's saying that the &quot;desirable state&quot; is being a bigot. Humans are desirable + all humans are bigots.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now personally I don't go for the transsexual metaphor as strongly as some people. I know that the original reason for Disquiet was because everyone who could see the monster in Mary Shelly's Fraknenstien feared and hated him, so I don't really think it's far to say &quot;well you could look at it in a different way, and if you do the metaphor becomes uncomfortable, therefore <u>bad</u>&quot;. But I do understand why some people dislike this facet of Promethean.<br /> <br /> Now my personal solution is to keep Disquiet because that is the way it happened in Mary Shelly's book but introduce more pro-human themes to try and take the edge off it. I'd start with a mortal-only merit called &quot;Civilised Morality&quot; designed to represent the things that people say are good about civilisation. It helps you overcome disquiet and combined with high expression <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ShamingTheMob\" target=\"_blank\">you can use it to quell disquiet in others</a>. So you could have a scientist saying &quot;I instinctively want to blame that stranger, but when I think rationally I know the problems began months before he arrived in town&quot;, or a priest turning to a Disuquiet fuelled mob and saying &quot;let he who is without sin cast the first stone&quot; and actually curing them of Disquiet.<br /> <br /> That would turn the metaphor from &quot;humanity is a species of bigots&quot; to &quot;humans' natural instincts are tribalistic and primitive - but they've found ways to become better than that.&quot; I think that's a cool message, and probably cooler than the current way Promethain is selling humanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:37:23-07:00","id":289885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I liked the point brought up in another thread recently: Disquiet is the human reaction ot Torment. Put another way, Prometheans have inherent emotional problems that mortals subconsciously pick up on and react to: the emotional problems are represented by Torment, and the mortal response is represented by Disquiet: they\u2019re two sides of the same coin. </div> </div> </div>Humans aren\u00b4t the only ones who react badly to disquiet. Is Nature itself who turns agains Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T13:28:34-07:00","id":289925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289884#post289884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the things that people say are good about civilisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>To help with this, I might recommend a book I remember positively: <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Search-Civilization-Remaking-Tarnished-Idea/dp/1555975801/\" target=\"_blank\">In Search of Civilization</a>. It's short, but it's also at home, so I can't really go leaf through it to give a quick summary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T15:48:27-07:00","id":290066,"title":"","content":"Maybe Azothic Memory will play a role in more than just the Pilgrimage. Like, &quot;Oh, hey. This guy's a jerk but it's because I'm a monster.&quot; Rather than, &quot;I have no idea why everyone around me hates me&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T15:52:32-07:00","id":290073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=290066#post290066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Azothic Memory will play a role in more than just the Pilgrimage. Like, &quot;Oh, hey. This guy's a jerk but it's because I'm a monster.&quot; Rather than, &quot;I have no idea why everyone around me hates me&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a roll for that. It keyed off of Empathy for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T15:56:00-07:00","id":290077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=290066#post290066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Azothic Memory will play a role in more than just the Pilgrimage. Like, &quot;Oh, hey. This guy's a jerk but it's because I'm a monster.&quot; Rather than, &quot;I have no idea why everyone around me hates me&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather hope it remains a mystery. Puzzling out their nature and coming to their own conclusions is part of a Prommie's early life cycle, I'd have to have it &quot;solved&quot; with a dice roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T16:54:22-07:00","id":290106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=290077#post290077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather hope it remains a mystery. Puzzling out their nature and coming to their own conclusions is part of a Prommie's early life cycle, I'd have to have it &quot;solved&quot; with a dice roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't mix up my pointing out the existence of a dice-roll in 1e's mechanics for a Promethean to avoid a Torment trigger by determining whether someone's behavior was owed to Disquiet with reseru's bit of guesswork that makes no reference to dice whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T17:04:09-07:00","id":290108,"title":"","content":"I thought Azothic Memory was new to 2e. Unless you meant the merit that meant you remembered some things from the bits you were made from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T17:17:16-07:00","id":290116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=290108#post290108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Azothic Memory was new to 2e. Unless you meant the merit that meant you remembered some things from the bits you were made from?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean there is specifically a 1e mechanic for determining &quot;this guy's a jerk but it's because I'm a monster&quot; on account of that conclusion's truth value setting whether or not a given negative interaction risks Torment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T17:22:13-07:00","id":290138,"title":"","content":"No, no. A Promethean who knows about Disquiet (I mean really knows, on a factual level) should absolutely get that resistance bonus for Torment (when applicable). No miscommunication there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T20:04:49-07:00","id":290961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289884#post289884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I'd argue that the problem is that disquiet is a metaphor for things that should be downplayed in a game that's supposed to celebrate humanity - but instead of being downplayed it's applied to the entire human population.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about all of this that's missing is that the Promethean relationship with humanity is all kinds of fucked up, and it's not the fault of either side. The fault lies in the unnatural state of Azoth burning within each and every one of the Created. Azoth is unnatural. It is anathema to all nature. Look at page 38 of <b>Promethean: the Created</b> to read about just <i>HOW</i> that occurs. Humans (and things that were once humans like vampires and werewolves) have no more CHOICE in experiencing Disquiet than the plants, animals, the very earth around one of the Created has. That's the curse, but it's also the hope...<br /> <br /> The final outcome of the Magnum Opus isn't to become a 'weak, fragile, bigoted' human being; it's rather a chance to become a being that can CHOOSE to be whatever one wishes to be! A Promethean has no choice but to be a monster, to be hated, to be rejected by everything around her, but a human? Well, that's a different circumstance altogether.<br /> <br /> ...At least, that's the crux of MY buy-in to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T20:14:13-07:00","id":290968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=290961#post290961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about all of this that's missing is that the Promethean relationship with humanity is all kinds of fucked up, and it's not the fault of either side. The fault lies in the unnatural state of Azoth burning within each and every one of the Created. Azoth is unnatural. It is anathema to all nature. Look at page 38 of <b>Promethean: the Created</b> to read about just <i>HOW</i> that occurs. Humans (and things that were once humans like vampires and werewolves) have no more CHOICE in experiencing Disquiet than the plants, animals, the very earth around one of the Created has. That's the curse, but it's also the hope...<br /> <br /> The final outcome of the Magnum Opus isn't to become a 'weak, fragile, bigoted' human being; it's rather a chance to become a being that can CHOOSE to be whatever one wishes to be! A Promethean has no choice but to be a monster, to be hated, to be rejected by everything around her, but a human? Well, that's a different circumstance altogether.<br /> <br /> ...At least, that's the crux of MY buy-in to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And for the sake of emphasis/repetition, the &quot;is this person acting this way because of Disquiet?&quot; check for Torment only lets a trigger through if the answer to &quot;is this person striving against me as a direct effect of my being an unholy abomination against nature?&quot; is &quot;Yes&quot; - you're not driven to despair of ever changing your lot in life from the knowledge that somebody just doesn't like you because of personal quirks, for all that they might rationalize their behavior as such later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T05:57:35-07:00","id":291220,"title":"","content":"While the description doesn't emphasise this factor, Disquiet affects more than just humans' attitudes to the Promethean - that's the focal point, but it also frays humans' relationships with one another. While comparisons between Disquiet and Torment have been made in this thread, it's also worth comparing Disquiet with the Wasteland: humanity is a desirable state, not least for its capacity for community, but the presence of a Promethean worries at that capacity; in essence, the nature of a Promethean damages <i>what's desirable</i> about humanity. Prometheans want to be part of the world, but they burn the world around them, turning it into waste. They want community and companionship, but they fray those things apart by their presence, until the only defence is to drive them away. They want to be whole and complete beings, but their nature forces them to lash out at the themselves, others, and the world at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T08:51:51-07:00","id":291383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=290968#post290968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for the sake of emphasis/repetition, the &quot;is this person acting this way because of Disquiet?&quot; check for Torment only lets a trigger through if the answer to &quot;is this person striving against me as a direct effect of my being an unholy abomination against nature?&quot; is &quot;Yes&quot; - you're not driven to despair of ever changing your lot in life from the knowledge that somebody just doesn't like you because of personal quirks, for all that they might rationalize their behavior as such later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans rationalise behaviour, but Azoth burns all around the same. The idea that all Prometheans have the same reaction to human ignorance and fear is laughable, since the effects of Azoth's unnatural flame manifests differently for each Lineage through the imbalanced Humours, so Disquiet, Wasteland, and Torment vary as well. But that's not the worst of it.<br /> <br /> It's the Azoth itself that drives the Created towards the New Dawn, or rather, it's the Principle that does. My take has been that the Principle represents the part of the Azothic Constant (if I'm allowed to coin a phrase) that is capable of something like thought. Azoth is that it is, like some unnatural, unknowable but ever-present force akin to gravity in the natural world; it can be measured, be rationalised, but ultimately it eludes perfect understanding because... well, no one knows.<b>*</b> However, the Principle WANTS Prometheans to reach their New Dawn, and it's that drive that keeps the Pilgrimage moving forward.<br /> <br /> I can't say if the Second Edition bears this out, but my thoughts on what Matt's said about Azothic Memory fits with my interpretation. Despite all of the horribleness of humans \u2013 even magnified as it may be in the World of Darkenss \u2013 the Created are driven towards that transcendent state of the Magnum Opus, whether those Prometheans actually desire that state or not.<br /> <br /> <b>*</b>Note: Physics understands gravity, true; however, despite General Relativity's testable predictions, anomalies and oddities abound. I'm NOT a theoretical physicist, but these games aren't really based on proper rocket surgery, so I allow my dubious analogy to stand. ~ P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:19:19-07:00","id":291566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If that\u2019s a buy-in that a group doesn\u2019t want to make, that\u2019s fine!</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Am I the only one who found this line very strange? Surely the writers want to <i>create</i> buy-in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289487#post289487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really see how awareness of social justice issues would make one <i>more</i> fond of promethean, rather than less.<br /> <br /> I suspect we're probably coming at the core metaphors differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how it could lead to either perspective, depending on what you see the &quot;core metaphor&quot; as.<br /> <br /> If you see it as a game of self-determination and self-discovery - of becoming the person you want to, be regardless of your origins and <i>the entire universe</i> hating you - then if you're pro-SJ, you're much more likely to be fond of Promethean. On the other hand, if you're anti-SJ, that's not really a metaphor you're comfortable with.<br /> <br /> If, however, you see the game as about <i>abandoning</i> who you really are or could be in order too seek &quot;normality&quot; - choosing to transform yourself from an unnatural abomination, into a good old-fashioned man or woman with a white picket fence and 2.5 kids - then if you're anti-SJ, you're much more likely to be fond of Promethean. On the other hand, if you're pro-SJ, that's not really a metaphor you're comfortable with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=289884#post289884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I'd argue that the problem is that disquiet is a metaphor for things that should be downplayed in a game that's supposed to celebrate humanity - but instead of being downplayed it's applied to the entire human population.<br /> <br /> Essentually it's saying that the &quot;desirable state&quot; is being a bigot. Humans are desirable + all humans are bigots.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now personally I don't go for the transsexual metaphor as strongly as some people. I know that the original reason for Disquiet was because everyone who could see the monster in Mary Shelly's Fraknenstien feared and hated him, so I don't really think it's far to say &quot;well you could look at it in a different way, and if you do the metaphor becomes uncomfortable, therefore <u>bad</u>&quot;. But I do understand why some people dislike this facet of Promethean.<br /> <br /> Now my personal solution is to keep Disquiet because that is the way it happened in Mary Shelly's book but introduce more pro-human themes to try and take the edge off it. I'd start with a mortal-only merit called &quot;Civilised Morality&quot; designed to represent the things that people say are good about civilisation. It helps you overcome disquiet and combined with high expression <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ShamingTheMob\" target=\"_blank\">you can use it to quell disquiet in others</a>. So you could have a scientist saying &quot;I instinctively want to blame that stranger, but when I think rationally I know the problems began months before he arrived in town&quot;, or a priest turning to a Disuquiet fuelled mob and saying &quot;let he who is without sin cast the first stone&quot; and actually curing them of Disquiet.<br /> <br /> That would turn the metaphor from &quot;humanity is a species of bigots&quot; to &quot;humans' natural instincts are tribalistic and primitive - but they've found ways to become better than that.&quot; I think that's a cool message, and probably cooler than the current way Promethain is selling humanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always seen Disquiet as the Promethean <i>doing things wrong </i>and offending people or weirding them out. It's an issue they kick themselves over, rather than a sad problem with everyone else.<br /> <br /> Not sure that's really supported by the rules yet, though. Just my personal way of reconciling the themes.<br /> <br /> (I'd call the Merit &quot;Charity&quot;, by the way. Excellent idea.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 10-24-2014, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:32:49-07:00","id":291575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=291566#post291566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I the only one who found this line very strange? Surely the writers want to <i>create</i> buy-in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Writers might. Fellows in humanity might feel less invested to push.<br /> <br /> THere was always this idea that Promethean was going to be a more niche game in an already niche market, so trying to push it too far invites more problems than it's worth..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:07:59-07:00","id":291605,"title":"","content":"The developer surely wants to attract people to the game, but altering its themes for the sake of pulling more people in isn't the right thing to do. You probably wouldn't do it either, were you in charge of your favorite game.<br /> <br /> No one likes a sell-out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T07:23:08-07:00","id":292010,"title":"","content":"Oh, I didn't mean changing the themes of the game. That would never work. But surely they want to get as much buy-in for those themes as possible, once they've been chosen? Just leaving it to chance seems ... odd.<br /> <br /> As if Starlord had said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hey, guys, I'm gonna fight Ronan. Want to come?<br /> <br /> Oh, you'd rather not die? Fine, fine risking your life is part of the concept, if you can't buy into that it's cool. I'll just go fight him by myself, all alone, then. </div> </div> </div>Anyway, did anyone else find it interesting that the Pristine Order of the Auric Chalice writeup implied that Alchemy is &quot;available to anyone&quot; as a result of of &quot;electronic communication, scanned grimoires, mass-produced glassware, and online chemical suppliers&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 10-25-2014, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T08:28:16-07:00","id":292047,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind they were talking in terms of how Resources used to be necessary back in the day, but not anymore \u2014 <i>not</i> whether or not any other preconditions exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T09:29:02-07:00","id":292995,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> OK, I actually think these guys are actually pretty sympathetic - the writeup maybe went too far in making it super-clear that they're not intended as the <i>good guys</i>, like Marvel's Civil War did with the pro-registration side.<br /> <br /> The unscrupulous scientist desperate for funding is a stock character in science fiction. So is the project leader who overrules his underlings who warn him that It's Not Ready. So is the overlooked glory-hound who will finally Show Them All when they cure death or whatever.<br /> <br /> I think what these guys are afraid of is, say, the Lizard from the Amazing Spider-Man film: someone who, afraid that they're going to run out of money before they've completed their (Great) work, uses an unfinished and dangerous prototype ... and ends up creating monsters.<br /> <br /> And they're right! That sort of thing is how you end up summoning Lillithim, creating Pandorans and, I dunno, whatever it is that Alchemists do that &quot;turns them into monsters&quot; in exchange for superpowers.*<br /> <br /> It's just that it never occurs to them that the <i>poverty</i> is the problem, not the poor people taking risks to escape it. They're policing in the right place, but not addressing the underlying problem. (Hey, like actual police!)<br /> <br /> *(Hey, is the Hulk an Alchemist character? That would be awesome. Very Promethean.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 10-26-2014, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T14:05:48-07:00","id":293175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=292995#post292995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*(Hey, is the Hulk an Alchemist character? That would be awesome. Very Promethean.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I would tend to say &quot;no&quot; to that... only because the traditional origin for the Hulk is that he was transformed by an accident (or at least outside forces). I know the Bill Bixby/Lou Ferigno TV series and the Incredible Hulk movie went with the idea that he was exposed as a result of intentionally experimenting on himself, in which case that might well work for an alchemist character.<br /> <br /> The Hulk himself, on the other hand, is very much a Promethean type of character, particularly if you view the transformation between Banner and Hulk as a metaphor for Torment. A stranger wanders into town, mostly keeping to himself until somebody, for one reason or another (Disquiet) gets confrontational with him... and makes him angry. Suddenly he becomes a raging, Disfigured monster, leaving a trail of destruction in his wake, and when he finally comes back to himself he has to either deal with the aftermath of his actions or move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T14:30:29-07:00","id":293205,"title":"","content":"The Hulk was created by an experiment gone wrong, actually: the detonation of the Gamma Bomb was no accident; only Banner\u2019s proximi. to it when it detonated was unintended. Also, there was a fan-splat written up some time ago about &quot;tieresians\u201d, which basically used Promethean metaphysics as a backdrop for Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde. In 2e terms, that sounds exactly like the sort of thing an alchemist might do in pursuit of transcending humanity that turns him into a monster. Another example would be the Invisible Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T16:31:13-07:00","id":293292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=288818#post288818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: On further thought, it especially bugs me because so much else in the game is geared toward showing what a shitshow humans are. Disquiet is basically a dramatic way of conveying the message &quot;Humans are stupid, violent bullies that react in the worst way possible to things that are different&quot;. Given that, the moral of this &quot;humanistic&quot; tale seems to be &quot;aspire to fit in, so we'll stop tormenting you&quot;, which is a metaphor that I find perhaps even more uncomfortable than some of Changeling's themes, which I didn't previously think possible. It looks at the tale of Frankenstein's monster, and validates the villagers with pitchforks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take the opposite view on the validating the villagers mostly because most prometheans aren't going to be with the villagers. They are going to be with the leapers. The other sections of humanity that fall under of the same alienation (though less disquiet fueled) that differ from social norms and suffer under the shadow of the majority. Minorities such as African Americans, Hispanics, Gays and Trans all suffer the same &quot;Get with the program or we'll be beat the living crap out of you&quot; but still those communities exist and are quite rich for milestone mining for Promethean games. Nearly all cultures have the disenfranchised, the distraught, and the outcasts and Promethean naturally gravitates to them and nothing binds people together like shared suffering.<br /> <br /> It's through this shared suffering that Promethean really shines as it starts asking &quot;Who am I and who do I wish to be?&quot;. Topics of gender identity, politics, and more start coming into formation by direct experience the Promethean has and plays into the milestones. It's starts asking harder and harder questions. The nature of the Divine, The nature of self sacrifice for a group, The purpose of life it's self and more.<br /> <br /> If they wish to be something more than human, they're more than certainly willing to have a go but even then there are mile stones. The nature of power, Should the strong care for the weak? Should humanity even be worth attempting if they are such pitiful bullies all the time and if so, why? (not that we don't already have a game about Transhumanism, it's called Mage but it would be interesting to see how Promethean deals with it.), What happens if you fully lose the humanity you had to begin with (Vampire) or even if you start to consider yourself human to begin with (Werewolf).<br /> <br /> The theme of Alienation is quite a disturbing one and one which the game hammers home quite well but overall, to use a metaphor, the game isn't validating the guards in the death camp but rather the humanity of the minorities inside it. The minorities that share in the same isolation and stigma that Prometheans deal with and while the game should make more effort in highlighting it, it is a natural starting point of where most Promethean games end up.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 10-26-2014, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T21:42:40-07:00","id":293388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=293292#post293292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take the opposite view on the validating the villagers mostly because most prometheans aren't going to be with the villagers. They are going to be with the leapers. The other sections of humanity that fall under of the same alienation (though less disquiet fueled) that differ from social norms and suffer under the shadow of the majority. Minorities such as African Americans, Hispanics, Gays and Trans all suffer the same &amp;quot;Get with the program or we'll be beat the living crap out of you&amp;quot; but still those communities exist and are quite rich for milestone mining for Promethean games. Nearly all cultures have the disenfranchised, the distraught, and the outcasts and Promethean naturally gravitates to them and nothing binds people together like shared suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>But these \u201coppressed minorities\u201d suffer from Disquiet every bit as much as the \u201coppressive majority\u201d does. This runs counter to the \u201cbound together by shared suffering\u201d idea. <br /> <br /> Who <i>doesn\u2019t</i> suffer from Disquiet? In 1e, ghosts, spirits, and <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s fetches, plus Prometheans and other Pyros-based creatures. And even there, 1e describes spirits being hostile toward Prometheans even without Disquiet to push them in that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T23:24:11-07:00","id":293501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=293388#post293388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But these \u201coppressed minorities\u201d suffer from Disquiet every bit as much as the \u201coppressive majority\u201d does. This runs counter to the \u201cbound together by shared suffering\u201d idea. </div> </div> </div> </div>Every metaphor breaks down, the closer it gets to reality. But even here, opposed minorities don't find solidarity across demographics, they find it within their own. Press those demos together, make them fight for resources, and you will see no unity between them. This is why gangs proliferate in prison, for example, or why pink triangles were bottom of the heap in the camps.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean it's not a useful lens. A throng is its own society, cast against mortals and others who would crush them, for no other reason than their differences. Disquiet works well to communicate the &quot;feel&quot; of oppression, but it flattens the various &quot;isms&quot; that are at work. Sexism is a different beast than racism, and both are separate from the classism, ableism, homophobia, sizeism, and ageism that cut across those lines. And a Promethean can be on the wrong side of none, any, or all of these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T01:06:46-07:00","id":293549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=293388#post293388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But these \u201coppressed minorities\u201d suffer from Disquiet every bit as much as the \u201coppressive majority\u201d does. This runs counter to the \u201cbound together by shared suffering\u201d idea.<br /> <br /> Who <i>doesn\u2019t</i> suffer from Disquiet? In 1e, ghosts, spirits, and <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s fetches, plus Prometheans and other Pyros-based creatures. And even there, 1e describes spirits being hostile toward Prometheans even without Disquiet to push them in that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st edition paints a bleak picture but honestly, using Disquiet as a cudgel for <u><i><b>every single human interaction </b></i></u>is both painful for storytelling and gets in the way of the theme of discovering humanity if used too much. As a houserule (for my one time actually setting up the game), I've ruled that disquiet affects first impressions, on how well said promethean is blending in with the subculture, and shared suffering that said peers of that subculture experience with the promethean. Shared suffering and experience, for better or for worse, does lay the foundation of including binding people into groups. especially if those groups are being persecuted.<br /> <br /> In such groups, I've typically greatly slowed down the clock for disquiet for prometheans PCs to capitalize on the social trust that they have earned long enough for them to get a few milestones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:35:09-07:00","id":293692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Verge:</b> Sexism is a different beast than racism, and both are separate from the classism, ableism, homophobia, sizeism, and ageism that cut across those lines. And a Promethean can be on the wrong side of none, any, or all of these. </div> </div> </div>Disquiet's also a dark childhood (especially a dark Victorian childhood) thing in that the world can be confusing, scary, running on rules you don't understand, and populated by adults who become suddenly and unfathomably angry with you in a way they never seem to do with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T07:21:30-07:00","id":293710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/288738-promethean-dev-blog-the-buy-in?p=293692#post293692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disquiet's also a dark childhood (especially a dark Victorian childhood) thing in that the world can be confusing, scary, running on rules you don't understand, and populated by adults who become suddenly and unfathomably angry with you in a way they never seem to do with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's terrific. That also puts Prometheans on a track parallel to runaways, kids risking the streets because home life's worse. Easily victimized, slow to trust, skeptical of all help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T08:20:40-07:00","id":293737,"title":"","content":"I hadn't thought of this when I first made my previous post, but you could also tie Redemption into the cycle of abuse concept - will be Promethean perpetuate it or break it once they become human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}